hin their four-year window. That is why many boxes start at 0.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 5 of 5 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2017: mean 0.38, median 0.07, top work 2.05. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Still counting: works from 2023–2026 have not completed their four-year citation window, so their values will rise. Do not compare them with older years yet.","Small base: the values for 2016, 2018, 2022 and 2024–2025 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2014 has fewer than 10 works (2014: 2), too few for a box. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2015–2023 have a median of 1–5.5 citations each; the highest median (5.5) is in 2017.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2017 have at least 21 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2025–2026 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 6 of 6 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2017: mean 9.7, median 5.5, top work 64. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Recent years: works from 2024–2026 have had less than three years to be cited, so their values will rise.","Small base: the values for 2016, 2018, 2022 and 2024–2025 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2014 has fewer than 10 works (2014: 2), too few for a band. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."]}}}